# Who owns what (Paulo, 2026-11-28: "can we have intuition and clock what we're orchestrating together?")

Several agents (Cursor, Claude sessions, the HQ) work in this repo at once. When two of them edit the same
files, each one undoes the other and Paulo ends up re-testing the same thing for hours. So every area has ONE
owner. If you are not the owner:

1. Do **not** edit the owner's files, not even "a small fix".
2. Write the ask on the HQ board instead, with Paulo's words and what you saw:
   `python C:/Users/PVProductions/HOMEBASE/staging/office/claim.py "<your name>" "<the ask>"` (it routes to the owner),
   or tell Paulo in one line that it belongs to the owner.
3. Never commit files you didn't change (`git commit -- <your paths>` only). Never sweep another agent's
   uncommitted edits into your commit.

| Area | Files | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| Online play (rooms, join, QR, sync, voice, identity, Palotino map rooms) | `claude/js/mv2_net*.js`, `mv2_voice.js`, `mv2_identity.js`, `claude/js/vendor/peerjs*`, `scripts/probe-online*.mjs` | Claude session "MV2 online play" |
| Collision and anti-tunneling | `claude/js/beta_tunnel.js`, `collision_grid.js`, `scripts/probe-tunnel.mjs` | Claude session "MV2 QA" |
| Hit shapes and the Art Board | `claude/js/hitshapes.js`, `claude/art-board.html`, `claude/js/art-*.js`, `scripts/capture-*.mjs` | Claude session "MV2 shape hitboxes" |
| AI brother | `claude/js/beta_sibling.js` and the AI brother modules | Claude session "MV2 smart AI brother" |
| Audio and frame rate | `claude/js/audio.js`, `sfx_*.js`, `scripts/probe-perf-audio.mjs` | Claude session "Launch readiness" |

Everything else: claim it first with `claim.py`; whoever claims it owns it until it's done.

## Online play is tested as one journey, never patched by symptom

Before any online change is pushed, `npm run probe:online` must pass the whole journey:
the host on PC opens a room; a phone-sized guest joins by code, by link and by QR; both reach Palotino and
the map, enter the same stage, see and hit each other, and see items, shots and water; then disconnect,
rejoin, and a 15-minute wait. One failing step = not pushed. Do not push a fix for one step that breaks another.
